# Implementation Plan - Production Supabase Backend Integration for Josan Driver App

Connect the existing Josan Logistics Driver App (`React Native` / `Expo SDK 57`) to the shared production **Supabase backend** (`https://xewecflkzxgnczukaana.supabase.co`) used by the **Josan Logistics Admin Website**.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Architecture Requirement**: The Driver App and Admin Website are independent clients that communicate **exclusively** through the shared Supabase backend.
> - **Zero UI Redesign**: Existing screens, layouts, navigation, and components are preserved exactly as designed. Mock data is replaced with live Supabase database queries and Realtime subscriptions.

---

## Technical Audit & Discoveries

### 1. Existing Backend Discovered
- **Supabase Production Instance**: `https://xewecflkzxgnczukaana.supabase.co`
- **Database Schema**: 11 core tables defined in `supabase/schema.sql`:
  - `public.profiles`: User identity and roles (`ADMIN`, `DISPATCHER`, `DRIVER`, `CUSTOMER`).
  - `public.drivers`: Driver profile, vehicle assignment, duty status, telematics (`id`, `profile_id`, `name`, `phone`, `email`, `vehicle_plate`, `current_latitude`, `current_longitude`, etc.).
  - `public.shipments`: Consignment records with tracking numbers, assigned `driver_id`, addresses, coordinates, timeline, and exact status values.
  - `public.trip_status_history`: Audit log tracking status changes with GPS timestamps.
  - `public.driver_locations`: Real-time GPS telematics stream with DB triggers updating `drivers.current_latitude/longitude`.
  - `public.proof_of_delivery`: Digital POD records with `signature_url`, `photo_url`, `receiver_name`, and timestamp.
  - `public.notifications`: System and user push/in-app alert records.

### 2. Mock & Fallback Data Identified
- `services/mockData.ts`: Contains static fallback data `MOCK_TRIPS` (`TRIP-2026-001`, `TRIP-2026-002`, `TRIP-2026-003`), `MOCK_PERFORMANCE`, `MOCK_DOCUMENTS`, `MOCK_NOTIFICATIONS`.
- `services/auth.ts`, `services/trips.ts`, `services/driver.ts`, `services/notifications.ts`: Had `__DEV__` fallback handlers returning mock data when REST endpoints failed.

### 3. Status Value Alignment
- Database constraint in `public.shipments`:
  `CHECK (status IN ('ASSIGNED', 'ACCEPTED', 'GOING_TO_PICKUP', 'ARRIVED_AT_PICKUP', 'PICKUP_COMPLETED', 'IN_TRANSIT', 'ARRIVED_AT_DELIVERY', 'DELIVERY_COMPLETED', 'CANCELLED'))`
- Update `types/trip.ts` `TripStatus` enum and mapping functions to enforce uppercase status values matching the backend and Admin Website.

